<p>Torrential rain in southeastern Brazil triggered flash flooding and landslides in Minas Gerais state, killing at least 23 to 30 people and leaving dozens missing as of Tuesday. Juiz de Fora and Ubá were among the hardest-hit areas. Officials said rivers burst their banks, streets turned into fast-moving currents, and homes and other buildings collapsed or were swept away after downpours that began on Monday. Rescue crews kept working through Tuesday. Firefighters, sniffer dogs, and residents searched mud and debris for survivors, while hundreds of people were forced from their homes.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/orIB43bBHpb246pGLCRksv9m7w3Uuxt7NQkT3QnCpl1pq0FHtJtOvJP77ZtHn7Y8sbVntZH61KLrok91T_S5tVwUwEHiYVer-4yy9vW0CL-Qygx6N4Jtn6axfH_mrSz0N3lWWwrQiqWRGQ049xSH41Ss0eLHZBrhwYeJvyYihzmgR1pTlQ' alt='Rescue teams search for victims amid debris after a landslide in Juiz de Fora, Minas Gerais, on February 24, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Hard-hit towns: Early official counts listed 16 deaths and 43 missing in Juiz de Fora, and seven deaths with four missing in Ubá.</li><li>Search challenges: At least 20 landslides were reported in isolated neighbourhoods, cutting off some areas and prompting officials to describe the situation as “extreme”.</li><li>Displacement: At least 440 people were reported displaced after the flooding and landslides.</li><li>Rescue toll: As searches continued Tuesday, some updates put the number of missing at 39, reflecting how counts can shift during rescue operations.</li><li>Record rainfall: Multiple outlets described the downpour as record rainfall for the month in the region, overwhelming waterways and triggering slope failures.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Residents searching for family: A local father told TV Globo he was digging through rubble for his six-year-old daughter, Sophia, and still hoped to find her alive. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975616/torrential-rains-leave-23-dead-in-brazil'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975616/torrential-rains-leave-23-dead-in-brazil'>Torrential rains leave 23 dead in Brazil</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/environment/article/2026/02/25/rescuers-search-for-missing-after-deluge-kills-at-least-30-in-brazil_6750855_114.html'>Rescuers search for missing after deluge kills at least 30 in Brazil</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/24/floods-landslides-brazil-kill-after-record-rainfall'>Floods and landslides in Brazil kill at least 30 after record rainfall</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/02/25/heavy-rains-leave-at-least-28-dead-and-dozens-missing-in-brazil-s-minas-gerais'>Heavy rains leave at least 28 dead and dozens missing in Brazil’s Minas Gerais</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c70k7vjllzeo'>Floods and landslides in Brazil kill at least 25</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/brazil-southeastern-region-severe-floods-deaths-evacuations-missing-persons-feb-25-2026/article70673883.ece'>Severe floods in southeast Brazil kill at least 25 and force hundreds to evacuate</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/24/at-least-23-dead-as-heavy-rains-unleash-floods-in-southeastern-brazil'>At least 23 dead as heavy rains unleash floods in southeastern Brazil</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260224-torrential-rains-leave-23-dead-in-brazil-dozens-missing'>Thirty people are killed, 43 others are reported missing and at least 440 are displaced from their homes after heavy rain triggers flash flooding in Juiz de Fora, Minas Gerais, Brazil. (AFP via France 24)</a> - france24.com</li></ul>